module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.absent_reads_identically_to_never_looked

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data absent_reads_identically_to_never_looked: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "absent_reads_identically_to_never_looked" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a search that never reached its subject returns exactly what a real absence returns** (an instrument that answers `zero occurrences` over a region it never actually read is not reporting a measurement, it is reporting its own miss in the vocabulary of a finding. The two states are indistinguishable in the output -- both are the empty result -- so the reader supplies the interpretation, and the interpretation that fits the question being asked is `absent`. ",

    "THREE SPECIMENS IN ONE NIGHT, TWO SESSIONS, THREE DIFFERENT WAYS OF MISSING THE SUBJECT (2026-09-04, gunbc#10197). WRONG PATH: joining main's 142 `gunbc#10254` admission rows against the tree to decide whether they were consumed, the witness module's file was derived from its module path as `dag/test/claim/spark/spark_oobe_screen_observation_witness.dag`; the real file is `..._witness_test.dag`. The read returned empty and the join reported 128 of 142 rows NOT bound to their target -- the answer that would have had 128 consumed rows CARRIED, and a carried consumed row is a stale admission, which refuses every unrelated pull request in the repository. WRONG WINDOW: a reviewer checking the same claim bounded the import read to lines 13-30 and got zero for the real spelling, because the import block runs well past line 30. WRONG DIRECTORY: an earlier check of the same night grepped `dag/product/...` for a symbol that lives under `dag/gunbc/product/...` and got nothing, which read as `the symbol does not exist` and nearly stood as a finding. ",

    "**THE TELL IS THAT A ZERO WAS ACCEPTED WITHOUT ANYTHING ESTABLISHING THAT THE INSTRUMENT RESOLVED ITS SUBJECT** -- no denominator, no positive control, no assertion that the file read was non-empty or that the window contained what it was supposed to contain. ",

    "The second specimen is the one that shows the shape cleanly: the reviewer ran a FAKE control spelling alongside the real one, got zero for both, and only that pairing revealed the window was wrong rather than the symbol absent. The control cost one extra line and was the entire difference between a measurement and a miss. ",

    "**RECOGNITION RULE: whenever an empty result is about to be read as evidence of absence, ask what the instrument would have returned had it never reached its subject; if that is the same value, the result carries no information and the absence is unestablished.** ",

    "THE REPAIR IS THAT THE INSTRUMENT MUST NOT BE ABLE TO RETURN A VALUE IT CANNOT SHOW IT RESOLVED. A positive control that must hit, or a denominator it must report -- a path read asserts the source is non-empty before its emptiness is allowed to mean anything, a windowed read asserts the window contains a known landmark, a directory search asserts the directory exists. A retry does not repair it: the same wrong path, window or directory returns the same empty result and agrees with itself. ",

    "FOURTH SPECIMEN, AND IT MOVES THE CLASS FROM OUR OWN ADDRESSING TO AN EXTERNAL TOOL'S (gunbc#10311, 2026-09-04). `gh run list --repo gunb-ai/gunbc --commit <11-character sha>` returned `[]` with EXIT 0; the same query with the full forty-character sha returned TWO runs -- a queued workflow_dispatch and a completed pull_request. Same head, same tool, same minute, reproduced independently by a second session on a different head within the hour. The three earlier specimens are all the caller mis-addressing its own read; this one is a tool ACCEPTING an identifier, failing to resolve it, and rendering that as a filter matching nothing. It is the same class because the same capability retires all four -- an instrument may not return a value it cannot show it resolved -- but it widens the population from reads we author to every external query keyed on an identifier. ",

    "**THE INPUT THAT BREAKS THE FOURTH SPECIMEN IS THE DEFAULT FORM IN WHICH WE HAND EACH OTHER SUBJECTS, WHICH IS WHAT MAKES IT A FLEET HAZARD RATHER THAN A TOOL QUIRK.** Every status message, review comment and hand-off in this repository quotes ten- and eleven-character shas, because that is what git prints and what prose wants. So the abbreviated form is not a careless variant a disciplined reader avoids -- it is the form the subject ARRIVES in. And the question it was asked was whether a healed head had been picked up for revalidation, which is exactly the question whose reassuring answer ends the investigation: the honest report would have been STRANDED, and the truth was merely QUEUED. ",

    "TRIGGER CONTRIBUTED BY THE FOURTH SPECIMEN, AND IT IS NARROWER AND MORE ACTUATABLE THAN A POSITIVE CONTROL: WHERE THE SUBJECT IS AN IDENTIFIER, CANONICALIZE IT BEFORE ASKING. For a git object that means forty characters, and it means treating ANY sha that arrived in prose as unresolved until expanded. That is decidable on our side even though the tool's behaviour is not ours to change -- DESIGN's outside-the-modeled-guarantee boundary bounds the CEILING at mechanically preventable for our own callers, and no higher. ",

    "BOUNDED AGAINST `empty_capture_read_as_clean_result`, which is the nearest neighbour and is NOT this: there the instrument DID refuse and said so, and the refusal merely travelled on a channel the reader did not keep, so the information exists and the repair is to keep the other stream. Here NO refusal exists anywhere, so there is no discarded diagnostic to recover. ",

    "Distinct from `denominator_moved_between_measurement_and_comparison`, where the instrument reached a real subject that had changed underneath it; here the subject never moved and was never reached. Both are cases of a number that describes the measuring rather than the measured, which is why neither is caught by re-running.)",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
